"answer": "Here is a summary of the emails regarding Project Zenith:\n\n1. **Introduction and Kick-off**: Project Zenith was introduced as a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics and optimizing cloud storage solutions. The kick-off was scheduled for June 15th (or July 15th in one email) with a phase one budget of $500,000. Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole were mentioned as leads.\n2. **Team Expansion**: The team was expanded to accelerate progress. Five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture were added, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Later, Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing) were welcomed.\n3. **Ideas and Development**: The project moved into a phase of gathering innovative ideas, particularly from R&D, to leverage AI in data visualization tools, with proposals due by July 20th. Following the design phase, the development phase began the following month, led by Omar Jensen.\n4. **Milestones and Feedback**: The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback was sought from stakeholders regarding the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November.\n5. **Budget Updates**: The compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000 to include additional training and third-party audits."
